SDL2: KMSDRM retries a refused async page flip on vblank

SPDX-License-Identifier: Zlib
Local alteration (v1.1.2 T3): the RK3326 kernel (4.4, Rockchip VOP)
reports DRM_CAP_ASYNC_PAGE_FLIP, but its atomic page flip helper refuses
DRM_MODE_PAGE_FLIP_ASYNC with EINVAL. An SDL2 GL app with swap interval 0
(GameMaker ports through gmloadernext, e.g. Dueling Dragons) then got
"Could not queue pageflip: -22" on every frame after the first and showed
a frozen or black screen. On that EINVAL SDL now drops the async flag for
the rest of the session and flips on vblank, as with vsync on.

--- a/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmopengles.c	2026-11-28 00:23:33.466136335 -0300
+++ b/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmopengles.c	2026-11-28 00:23:33.480196732 -0300
@@ -181,6 +181,16 @@
         ret = KMSDRM_drmModePageFlip(viddata->drm_fd, dispdata->crtc->crtc_id,
                                      fb_info->fb_id, flip_flags, &windata->waiting_for_flip);
 
+        /* A driver may report DRM_CAP_ASYNC_PAGE_FLIP and still refuse the
+           flag (EINVAL, the atomic page flip helper of older kernels):
+           flip on vblank from then on. */
+        if (ret == -EINVAL && (flip_flags & DRM_MODE_PAGE_FLIP_ASYNC)) {
+            viddata->async_pageflip_support = SDL_FALSE;
+            flip_flags &= ~DRM_MODE_PAGE_FLIP_ASYNC;
+            ret = KMSDRM_drmModePageFlip(viddata->drm_fd, dispdata->crtc->crtc_id,
+                                         fb_info->fb_id, flip_flags, &windata->waiting_for_flip);
+        }
+
         if (ret == 0) {
             windata->waiting_for_flip = SDL_TRUE;
         } else {
